<title>USA: USDA to raise ag inspection fees on September 1.</title>
<headline>USDA to raise ag inspection fees on September 1.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>User fees for U.S. agricultural quarantine and inspection services will be increased beginning September 1, the Agriculture Department said Thursday.</p>
<p>In a Federal Register notice, the USDA's Animal and Plant Health Inspection Service said it set a schedule of fees for fiscal years 1997 through 2002 based on the anticipated actual cost of the services.</p>
<p>The user fees pay for the use of USDA trained dogs, x-ray equipment and inspectors to examine trucks, ships, railroad cars and aircraft arriving at U.S. ports. The 1996 farm bill allows the USDA to increase fees to reflect the rising costs of inspection services, and to charge late payment penalties and interest.</p>
